  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `step_fit.rs`: the curved-face fit (#2600) measures every edge of the facets that it keeps, inside and boundary. It reports the highest edge height times a bound for the inside of a facet:\n  - cylinder: 1.0;\n  - cone, sphere, torus: 1.5 (the two-way bound is 4/3, from Waldron, SIAM J. Numer. Anal. 35, 1998; 1.5 adds a margin).\n- The import takes the larger of this value and the pass tolerance as the chord (`step.rs` was already `kept.tol.max(off)`; it is not changed).\n- The split limit of an inside edge is now `tol / kind.inside()`. Before, it was `2 x tol`, and the import reported `tol`.\n- `step_facets.rs`: one doc comment only.\n- Decision entry: `docs/decisions/2718-step-chord-kept-height.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\nBar fixture `bar_cross_holes.step` (chord that the import reports):\n\n| | chord |\n|---|---|\n| before (main) | 0.005 mm, while the kept wall edges stood up to about 0.01 mm off |\n| honest report, old `2 x tol` split | 0.00999 mm (over `CHORD_CAP` 0.005 mm: reduced fidelity) |\n| after (this PR) | 0.005 mm |\n\nSynthetic faces (unit pins, `TOL` 0.005 mm). The lattice boundary edges are not split, so they set the worst value. Before this PR the fit reported 0 for each face, and the import reported 0.005 mm.\n\n| face | reported after | sampled worst of the kept facets |\n|---|---|---|\n| cylinder R10 | 0.00800 mm | 0.00800 mm |\n| cone 30 deg | 0.02121 mm | 0.01225 mm |\n| sphere R10 | 0.01153 mm | 0.00751 mm |\n| torus 20/5, outer | 0.01190 mm | 0.00794 mm |\n| torus 20/5, inner (saddle) | 0.01079 mm | 0.00683 mm |\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/app/src/geometry/import/step_fit_tests.rs` (lib):\n- `a_cylinder_face_reports_no_less_than_its_facets_stand_off`\n- `a_cone_face_reports_no_less_than_its_facets_stand_off`\n- `a_sphere_face_reports_no_less_than_its_facets_stand_off`\n- `a_torus_face_reports_no_less_than_its_facets_stand_off`\n\nEach asserts that the sampled worst is over `TOL` (the old report), that the reported value is not below it, and that the reported value is not more than 2 times it. The bar stays at full fidelity: `tilted_gouge::the_step_bars_wall_facets_lie_on_the_cylinder` (it fails with the honest report and the old split: `full fidelity: 0.009987214102760605`).\n\nQuick gate on head c8afe25f6: 22 steps, 0 failed. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `feature_edge_g1_join` (#2713, claimed by another contributor) is not in the quick plan of this diff. This PR does not change its expected values.\n- No real STEP model with a cone, sphere or torus face; those kinds are pinned with synthetic meshes only.\n- Facet counts on large models: the tighter split makes more facets. A face that runs out of facet budget keeps its larger edges and reports them (reduced fidelity, not a silent pass).\n- Release-lane and heavy tests.\n\nChangelog: STEP import now reports how far the kept curved facets stand off their surface, and splits them to the import tolerance, so a model is not marked full fidelity when its facets are coarser.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2718\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
